<title>UK: Daewoo ready to buy Lotus Group - FT.</title>
<headline>Daewoo ready to buy Lotus Group - FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea's Daewoo Motor Co is ready to pay a substantial premium to buy British sportscar maker and auto engineer Lotus Group, the Financial Times said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The paper said that under the terms of the deal, which could be signed by the end of the week, Daewoo is expected to pay in the region of $75 million to Romano Artioli, the chairman and owner of the group.</p>
<p>This would represent more than other potential buyers were willing to pay for Lotus, the paper added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
